{
  "purpose": "Qualify tracked primary/RTX RTP accounting without deducting untracked FlexFEC from the native GCC target",
  "revision": "7c206805cca1f4fcb5d89fdc73ea02605a8501be",
  "passed": false,
  "referenceConfigurationChanged": false,
  "udpSocketLimitsRestored": {
    "receiveBytes": 212992,
    "sendBytes": 212992
  },
  "ownedContainersRemoved": true,
  "interpretation": [
    "The unchanged 3-second down-hold profile now returns from 360p through 540p to 720p30 in both direct and adaptive MediaMTX delivery. Both complete runs pass format and source-bitrate recovery gates. Previously they remained at 360p after 90 seconds.",
    "Both unchanged-profile runs still fail playback during the initial capacity drop: MediaMTX has 2.798 seconds of total disruption including 1.268 seconds after the transition window; direct has 3.149 seconds of disruption. Neither drops decoded frames or freezes during recovery.",
    "Changing only downHold from 3 seconds to 1 second gives one complete MediaMTX pass, with 1.870 seconds of transition freezes and no steady/recovery freezes. The identical repeat returns to 720p but fails playback: 2.038 seconds total disruption includes a 0.579-second late freeze. The faster setting is not promoted as stabilized.",
    "The direct fast-down trial is incomplete because the collector cannot read the phase-control file at the end of recovery. Its last observations show 720p30 and 6 Mbit/s, but they cannot replace complete gates. The underlying file-visibility cause remains unproven.",
    "All four complete cases preserve one encoder/session, configured cadence, minimum dwell and sampled media-time continuity. The 3-second freeze/disruption bound and 4-second transition window were not relaxed. These are not capture-to-display latency or hardware qualification results.",
    "The accounting correction is independently reproduced by a deterministic primary/FEC writer and TWCC regression: the acknowledged rate includes tracked RTP headers and payload, excludes untracked FEC, and must not have the FEC ratio deducted again. The pacer retains the configured repair budget exactly once.",
    "Remaining work is transition-fluidity stabilization, robust phase-file delivery in the test harness, repeated direct/MediaMTX/TURN qualification and resource/latency measurements."
  ],
